* Marshall Silver Jubilee 2555 100 W power amp, transcribed from the factory drawing 2555 STD (drtube.com/schematics/marshall/2555amp.gif and 2555psu.gif): a long-tailed
* ECC83 phase inverter (V3) with the negative feedback and the presence network, four EL34 with fixed bias as two parallel pairs, the output transformer and the HT supply
* (the choke T2, C35 50u twice and R51 / R50 10k feeding the phase inverter and the preamp rail A).
*
* Assumptions where the drawing is silent or ambiguous (change them here, not in code):
*  - plate a (82k, R45) drives the pair V4 / V5 (grids through R58 / R59 5k6) and plate b (100k, R46) the pair V6 / V7 (R60 / R61 5k6);
*  - C15 (47p) is between the two coupled grid lines, as drawn;
*  - the negative feedback (R44 100k, the "Pur" wire) is taken from the 4 ohm tap into the feedback node y (between R17 10k and R20 4k7); the presence network is C14 0.1u,
*    the presence rheostat VR7 (22k linear, wiper tied to its end) and R19 10 ohm from y to ground, in parallel with R20;
*  - the bias supply (a heater-winding source through R48 27k and D10, filtered by C17 10u) is a source behind 27k; the divider R47 15k / RV1 22k trimmer (at 11k) / R23 56k sets
*    the grids, C16 10u filters it; the figure is calibrated for about 35 mA per tube;
*  - the output transformer (TX 784-139) and the HT figures are not on the drawing: copied from the JCM900; the High / Low (pentode / triode) switch S3 is not modelled (High);
*  - the screens take their HT through R53 to R56 (1k5 each) from the choke output.

.nodes pin ga kc z y gb pa pb d1 d2 bm bias g45 g67 s45 s67 sb pt pbm npt npb a t16 t8 bk x j2 nb pr pr2 rv

S VAUDIO pin 1k 0
S VHT a 1 485
S VBIAS nb 27k -71

* Phase inverter V3: C28 .022 into the first grid, the second grid coupled by C29 0.1u to the feedback node y; both grids returned through 1M to the node z under R40 470.
C C28 pin ga 22n
R R39 ga z 1M
R R41 gb z 1M
C C29 gb y 0.1u
T V3A ga pa kc 12AX7
T V3B gb pb kc 12AX7
R R40 kc z 470
R R17 z y 10k
R R20 y 0 4k7
R R45 j2 pa 82k
R R46 j2 pb 100k

* Presence: C14 in series with the rheostat VR7 (22k linear, more resistance, less presence) and R19, from y to ground.
C C14 y pr 0.1u
R VR7 pr pr2 5k
R R19 pr2 0 10

* Coupling (C30 / C31 22n) to the two output pairs, their 220k grid returns to the bias line bm, and C15 between the grid lines.
C C30 pa d1 22n
C C31 pb d2 22n
C C15 d1 d2 47p
R R21 d1 bm 220k
R R22 bm d2 220k
R R47 bm nb 15k
R RV1 bm rv 11k
R R23 rv 0 56k
C C16 bm 0 10u
C C17 nb 0 10u

* EL34s: each pair shares the grid stoppers (5k6 per tube), the screen resistors (1k5 per tube) and the plate load.
R RG45 d1 g45 5k6/2
R RG67 d2 g67 5k6/2
P V4_5 g45 pt s45 0 EL34 2
P V6_7 g67 pbm s67 0 EL34 2
R R53_54 sb s45 1k5/2
R R55_56 sb s67 1k5/2

* Output transformer (taken as the JCM900's; its centre tap is on a): plate-to-plate 1.9k, 3.5 H per primary half; windings are primary halves, then the 16R, 8R and 4R sections of the secondary.
R DCR_PT pt npt 40
R DCR_PB pbm npb 40
.param n16 = 2*1/sqrt(1900/16)
.xfmr OT L=3.5 SAT=4.7
  W npt a 1 pri
  W a npb 1 pri
  W t16 t8 0.2929*n16 sec
  W t8 bk 0.2071*n16 sec
  W bk 0 0.5*n16 sec
  K pri pri 0.9998
  K pri sec 0.9993
  K sec sec 0.9998
.end
R RLOAD t16 0 16

* Negative feedback from the 4 ohm tap (the "Pur" wire), 100k.
R R44 bk y 100k

* HT supply: the output transformer's centre tap is on a (the supply's reservoir C36 100u is modelled there); the choke T2 (about 100 ohm) leads to sb, which holds the
* screens and C35 50u, then R51 10k to the phase inverter's rail j2 (C35 50u) and R50 10k to the preamp rail A (x).
R TCH a sb 100
C C35A sb 0 50u
R R51 sb j2 10k
C C35B j2 0 50u
R R50 j2 x 10k
R RPREAMP x 0 56k
